QuestGuidance.Register("en",87,{
[2753]="7002D478\n1\tLocate Rhavameldir\tRhavameldir awaits you at the top of the second tower in Fornost.\n2\tDefeat Rhavameldir\tRhavameldir must be shown his place. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat Rhavameldir's minions.\tRhavameldir's minions must now be destroyed.\n",
[2754]="7002BBD3\n1\tJoin Saruman on the Peak of Orthanc\tJoin Saruman upon the Pinnacle of Orthanc.\n2\tDestroy Saruman's Ring\tYou must use the power of the five subservient rings to destroy Saruman's master ring. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2755]="7002BBD9\n1\tDefeat both Troll bosses in each wing (Tier 4 Fumes and Haze active)\tDo not defeat the leaders of the Abominations and Fire-orcs in the Pits of Isengard until in Tier 4 of Choking Haze and Toxic Fumes. Killing the fire and abomination monsters will advance the tier of the effect.\n",
[2756]="700276B2\n1\tDo not harm any tortured spirits\t\n",
[2757]="7003354A\n1\tApproach the Great Goblin's throne\tThe Great Goblin's throne lies deep within Goblin-town. His reign must be brought to an end quickly if the Free Peoples of Middle-earth are to remain safe.\n2\tDefeat the Great Goblin in under 4 minutes\tThe Great Goblin and his minions must be defeated with great haste if the Free Peoples of Middle-earth are to remain safe. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2758]="70044F8B\n1\tConfront the Gloom of Nurn\tYou must return Earnil and Mardil to rest swiftly while battling the Gloom of Nurn. The Gloom of Nurn seeks to claim the crown of the King for Gothmog, who has returned to reclaim the throne of Gondor after his long absence.\n2\tDefeat Earnil and Mardil with haste after they are summoned\tYou must return Earnil and Mardil to rest swiftly while battling the Gloom of Nurn. The Gloom of Nurn seeks to claim the crown of the King for Gothmog, who has returned to reclaim the throne of Gondor after his long absence. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat the Gloom of Nurn\tYou must now defeat the Gloom of Nurn. The Gloom of Nurn seeks to claim the crown of the King for Gothmog, who has returned to reclaim the throne of Gondor after his long absence.\n",
[2759]="7002CDB9\n1\tProtect all the Forest Roots\tGurthúl has unleashed her venomous spiderlings upon the roots of the forest. You must prevent any roots from being corrupted by their poison to ensure the forest above remains healthy. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2760]="70022B4A\n1\tFind Sambrog\tSambrog can be found in the greatest depths of the Great Barrow.\n2\tDisturb the crypt\tSambrog can be found in the greatest depths of the Great Barrow. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat Sambrog\tSambrog hates those who disturb and defile his crypt.\n",
[2761]="700459C0\n1\tConfront Rakothas\tRakothas is a deadly foe, and to overpower him without the use of more than one powder keg would add shame to his defeat.\n2\tDefeat Rakothas using only one powder keg\tRakothas is a deadly foe, and to overpower him without the use of more than one powder keg would add shame to his defeat. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2762]="700607AF\n1\tComplete 'A Flurry of Fireworks' without letting any fireworks launch early!\t\n2\tComplete 'A Flurry of Fireworks' without letting any fireworks launch early!\t\n",
[2763]="700607AA\n1\tComplete 'A Flurry of Fireworks' without letting any fireworks launch early!\t\n2\tComplete 'A Flurry of Fireworks' without letting any fireworks launch early!\t\n",
[2764]="700249BF\n1\tProceed to the stagnant pool\tThe poisoned waters must gather into a stagnant pool at some point.\n2\tDefeat the Huorns\tOnce a Huorn has marked you with sap, do not replace it with the other Huorn's sap. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2765]="700228B3\n1\tDefeat Storvâgûn\tStorvâgûn must be defeated without anyone being caught by the avalanche from the peak of Helegrod.\n",
[2766]="70043389\n1\tDefeat thirty Culvert Slugs in under thirty minutes\tThe tunnels beneath Osgiliath have many challengers - all of whom must be defeated with haste if Faramir is to be found.\n2\tDefeat Culvert Slugs in under thirty minutes (total: 30)\tThe tunnels beneath Osgiliath have many challengers - all of whom must be defeated with haste if Faramir is to be found. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2767]="70025608\n1\tDrugoth the Death-monger has relocated from the Misty Mountains and made his new home in the largest iceberg in the Icebay of Forochel. Now, his mad, rambling mind is planning an attack on Annúminas to the south. You must stop this attack before it happens. Proceed through the fortress and reach the summit of the glacier. Follow Drugoth, and put an end to his devious plot.\t\n2\tDefeat Drugoth\tHaving killed Drugoth's captains, you have reached the top of the iceberg and blocked the Death-monger's escape. You must defeat Drugoth as quickly as possible, while avoiding the interference of his two guardians. This challenge quest will fail if either guardian is defeated. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2768]="7004BCEA\n1\tThraknûl's main torture chamber houses many instruments of pain, as well as many holding cells for his victims.\t\n",
[2769]="70022B32\n1\tApproach Thadúr the Ravager\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow.\n2\tDefeat Thadúr the Ravager\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow.\n3\tUse the brazier\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tDefeat Thadúr the Ravager\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow.\n5\tUse the second brazier\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tDefeat Thardúr the Ravager\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow.\n7\tUse the final brazier\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n8\tDefeat Thardúr the Ravager\tThadúr the Ravager, an ancient Gaunt-lord, has arisen deep within the watery depths of the Great Barrow.\n",
[2770]="7001E683\n1\tDefeat Thaguzg\tYou should defeat Thaguzg without his minions' assistance. They must not reach him, or great woe will befall your fellowship.\n",
[2771]="70033C7F\n1\tDefeat Tabî-kohin without allowing any of the bells of Dale to fall\tDo not allow any of the bells to fall before Tabî-kohin has been defeated. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2772]="7002D418\n1\tFind Megoriath, the Wraith of Water\tThe wraith is waiting at the end of the water tower.\n2\tDefeat Megoriath\tMegoriath, the Wraith of Water, is awaiting you. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2773]="70051B72\n1\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff without any camp-fires going out\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff without any camp-fires going out.\n2\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff without any camp-fires going out.\t\n",
[2774]="70051B77\n1\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff without any camp-fires going out\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff without any camp-fires going out.\n2\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff without any camp-fires going out.\t\n",
[2775]="7001E681\n1\tDefeat Gorothúl\tGorothúl lies deep within Sammath Gûl, a chamber of Dol Guldur. You should defeat Gorothúl and attempt to unlock the doors behind which the spirit Demafaer resides.\n2\tDefeat Demafaer\tDemafaer stands guard within the chambers of the Necromancer. The great doors are unlocked; you should defeat the great fell spirit, Demafaer, servant of the Necromancer.\n",
[2776]="70051398\n1\tRetrieve Grár's bones\tRetrieve Grár's bones.\n2\tSurvive the Howling Pit\tSurvive the Howling Pit.\n3\tSurvive the Howling Pit\tSurvive the Howling Pit.\n4\tSurvive the Howling Pit\tSurvive the Howling Pit.\n5\tSurvive the Howling Pit\tSurvive the Howling Pit.\n",
[2777]="7001ECE1\n1\tDefeat the Lieutenant of Dol Guldur before his fell-beast steed falls\tThe Lieutenant of Dol Guldur stands at the top of Barad Guldur with the cruel fell-beast he rides from tower to tower. You should endeavour to defeat the Lieutenant of Dol Guldur before defeating his evil steed, a fell-beast of Mordor.\n",
[2778]="7001E68A\n1\tDefeat the Lost One\tThe Lost One is below the Sixteenth Hall, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. You have been challenged to prove your great worth by defeating the Lost One without making the battle easier by killing his summoned gredbyg.\n",
[2779]="7002371A\n1\tFind a way to enter Ferndúr's chamber\tFerndúr the Virulent remains scheming deep within the Rhudauran temple.\n2\tDestroy all the corpses before defeating Ferndúr\tFerndúr the Virulent has nearly completed his deadly experiments beneath the lost Rhudauran temple. The plagues he has concocted are too deadly to be allowed to fester. You must destroy all the corpses within his chamber before the Gaunt-lord himself is defeated in order to ensure that every trace of them is obliterated.\n",
[2780]="7004BD2D\n1\tConfront High Priest Dáuraga and High Priestess Khôkali\tThe Order of the Eye descended into the Abyss of Mordath to defeat the Firehorns and seek the lost artifacts of the Dark Lord, but instead they have found secrets more terrible than they dared imagine.\n2\tDefeat High Priest Dáuraga and High Priestess Khôkali after allowing them to harness the essence of each of the Spoiled\tYou and your fellows must allow the High Priest and High Priestess of the Order of the Eye to harness the essence of each of the Spoiled before defeating them. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2781]="7002712C\n1\tUse every Trap Mechanism in the caverns\030Use every Incantation Stone in the caverns\030Use every Suspicious Wall in the caverns\030Destroy every Pile of Bones in the caverns\tComplete the instance having used every Trap Mechanism, Suspicious Wall, and Incantation Stone and having destroyed every Pile of Bones.\n",
[2782]="70024C7B\n1\tFind Gortheron\tGortheron is at the highest tower of Ost Dunhoth. Once he is found, be prepared to stand against his forces.\n2\tAllow Gortheron to reach maximum power\tGortheron's forces are vast and varied. As Gortheron's army grows, so does he. Show Sauron that you do not fear him by defeating Gortheron the Doom-caller at the height of his power. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat Gortheron\tGortheron's forces are vast and varied. As Gortheron's army grows, so does he. Show Sauron that you do not fear him by defeating Gortheron at the height of his power. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2783]="7004BD2E\n1\tConfront King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns\tDesperate to reclaim Manthríf, King Váskmun Greytooth has led the Firehorns into the Abyss of Mordath, but where has the elusive Dwarf-ring come to rest?\n2\tDefeat Fingar the Greedy after fully overcoming every manifestation of Dragon-spell\tYou and your fellows must fully survive each of Fingar's manifestations of Dragon-spell before defeating the Worm of Angband. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2784]="700459C1\n1\tConfront Gothmog the Dread Terror\tGothmog the Dread Terror wields many fell powers, including the power of illusion. Only those who free themselves from his illusions swiftly will be able to stand against his might.\n2\tEscape from the Breach of Terror within 20 minutes\tGothmog the Dread Terror wields many fell powers, including the power of illusion. Only those who free themselves from his illusions swiftly will be able to stand against his might. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
